<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seimas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Seimas is the single-chamber parliament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, with 141 members elected for four-year terms under a mixed system. The name, taken from the diet of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>, was revived for the parliament of the interwar republic, which dominated government under the constitution of 1922 until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antanas-smetona">Antanas Smetona</a> dissolved it in 1927. The modern Seimas was established under the constitution of 1992.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seimas.jpg" alt="Seimas" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arvydas Každailis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seimas_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
